// Tataka's Wasteland — Bala Kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Bala Kanda, sargas 24-26 (verify)
// Staged for the Ramlila stage: a scene before and after the fight.

>> scene waste
>> music grief
>> light dim
>> cast vishvamitra at 0.66 face=left
>> cast rama:prince at 0.44
>> cast lakshmana:prince at 0.32
The emptied country. Nothing grows, and the wind carries grit.
>> shake 3
>> sound stompWarn
LAKSHMANA: The ground shook. She is close. I can smell the dust.
>> pose vishvamitra point
VISHVAMITRA: Do not hesitate, Rama. Protect this land and its people.
>> pose rama draw2
>> wait 0.6
>> battle tataka
>> scene road clear
>> music calm
>> light full
>> together
>> enter vishvamitra from right to 0.62 in 2
>> enter rama:prince from left to 0.42 in 1.8
>> enter lakshmana:prince from left to 0.3 in 1.6
>> wash
Tataka falls, and the wasteland can be lived in again.
>> pose vishvamitra raise
VISHVAMITRA: Now this country can be lived in again.
>> pose rama namaste
RAMA: Then it was right.
>> pose vishvamitra give
Pleased, Vishvamitra prepares to give Rama the divine astras.
-> END
